    {
      "id": "library/10665-360861/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Overview",
      "pageStart": 8,
      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/sec-002-overview.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "What is this technical brief?\nThis technical brief by the World Health Organization \n(WHO) updates and supplements previous WHO \nguidelines and guidance on pre-exposure prophylaxis \n(PrEP) for HIV prevention. The brief aims to support \ndifferentiated, simplified, demedicalized and \ncomprehensive PrEP services. This can support PrEP \nuptake, persistence and effective use and assist efforts \nto achieve global goals set out in the 2022–2030 Global \nHealth Sector Strategies on HIV, viral hepatitis and \nsexually transmitted infections. Further updates to \nWHO PrEP implementation guidance are expect",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Gives an overview of the technical brief, which updates WHO guidance to support differentiated, simplified, demedicalized PrEP services in line with the 2022–2030 global health sector strategies. It lists key points on starting and stopping oral PrEP, including event-driven dosing for people assigned male at birth not taking estradiol-based hormones, and on hepatitis B and C testing. It also introduces the four building blocks of differentiated delivery: where, who, when and what.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
