    {
      "id": "library/10665-360861/blocks/prose-sec-021",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Building blocks of differentiated PrEP service delivery",
      "pageStart": 24,
      "pageEnd": 24,
      "target": "../sections/sec-021-building-blocks-of-differentiated-prep-service-d.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "delivery\nIn many countries, individuals interested in PrEP \nmust go to a health care facility (often an HIV clinic) \nto obtain a prescription from a medical provider \n(often a physician). In recent years, and particularly \nduring the COVID-19 pandemic (60), the shift towards \ndifferentiated PrEP service delivery has accelerated.",
      "truncated": false,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Introduces differentiated PrEP delivery, noting the shift away from clinic-only physician prescribing that accelerated during COVID-19.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-360861/blocks/prose-sec-022",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Differentiated PrEP service delivery: When, where, who and what to deliver",
      "pageStart": 24,
      "pageEnd": 25,
      "target": "../sections/sec-022-differentiated-prep-service-delivery-when-where.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "delivery: When, where, who \nand what to deliver\nA differentiated PrEP service delivery approach \nis person- and community-centred and adapts \nservices to the needs and preferences of the people \nwho are interested in and could benefit from PrEP. \nDifferentiated PrEP service delivery may also support \nmore efficient and cost–effective use of health care \nresources. WHO recommends differentiated service \ndelivery for HIV testing and antiretroviral therapy \n(ART) (4). Delivery of person-centred health services is \none of the key strategic directions of the global health \nsector strategies on HIV,",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Defines differentiated PrEP service delivery as person- and community-centred and links it to the global health sector strategies. It presents the four building blocks (when, where, who and what), which can differ between initiation, continuation and re-initiation and across PrEP products.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-360861/blocks/prose-sec-023",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Where to deliver PrEP",
      "pageStart": 25,
      "pageEnd": 27,
      "target": "../sections/sec-023-where-to-deliver-prep.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "There are a range of barriers to PrEP access, uptake, \npersistence and effective use associated with service \ndelivery in health care facilities. These include actual \nor perceived lack of privacy, stigma and discrimination, \nnegative attitudes of health care providers, travel \ndistance, direct and opportunity costs for clients, \nfrequency of required clinic visits for continuation, \nlengthy waiting times and inconvenient operating \nhours. Provider-level barriers include policy and \nlegal barriers (for example, policies restricting \neligibility), lack of training, understaffing, limited \ntime",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out barriers to PrEP in health facilities, such as stigma, lack of privacy, distance, costs and long waits, as well as provider-side barriers. It argues that oral PrEP and the ring have few required components and can be delivered in community settings, while more research is needed for long-acting cabotegravir. Evidence and provider views on community-based delivery follow.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-360861/blocks/prose-sec-024",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "PrEP in fixed and mobile community settings",
      "pageStart": 27,
      "pageEnd": 29,
      "target": "../sections/sec-024-prep-in-fixed-and-mobile-community-settings.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Service models that deliver oral PrEP in fixed \ncommunity sites (such as through nongovernmental \norganizations) and mobile and semimobile sites (for \nexample, vans parked in community settings) have \nbeen implemented. A systematic review (Box 7) (63) \nidentified diverse models demonstrating the feasibility \nof these approaches in a range of countries, but data on \neffectiveness were limited. In addition to considerations \noutlined above, studies highlighted the need for \nstrong partnerships between mobile PrEP delivery \nsites and local community-based organizations. \nSame-day PrEP initiation",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes oral PrEP delivery in fixed and mobile community sites, such as NGO centres and vans, and the importance of partnerships with community organizations and integrated services. A box summarises review evidence, including the SEARCH trial in Kenya and Uganda and the Love O2O study in Thailand, and an example from Viet Nam is pictured.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
